## Active Technologies
- Rust 1.94 (workspace edition 2021) for backend crates; Functions V1.1 in `kalamdb-functions` (V8 152.2, ABI v2 async, V8-only) + `kalamdb-core` orchestration (`ActiveFunctionSet`, `FunctionExecutionRoot`); JS-boundary FlatBuffers in `kalamdb-serialization`
- Wire txs: **`BackendSessionManager` block API** (same as gRPC `BeginTransaction`/`Commit`); wire SQL data path: **`SqlExecutor`**; HTTP batch txs: **`RequestTransactionBatchGuard`** only
- Existing stack — `tokio`, `tonic`, `dashmap`, `datafusion` 55.x, `kalamdb-transactions`, `kalamdb-api`, `kalamdb-views`; **`pgwire`** workspace-pinned in `kalamdb-postgres-wire` only
- No `arrow-pg` in wire MVP — `row_encoder.rs` uses existing `ExecutionResult`/`RecordBatch`; optional encoder spike later
- Client catalog: **`pg_catalog` shim views** project from `system.*` (US9); not aliases; registered when `postgres_wire.enabled` is true
- Stability-first migration: preserve 027 behavior; regression gates per `specs/033-unified-backend-pgwire/quickstart.md`
- Connection sessions expose `origin` in `system.sessions`: `extension_bridge` | `wire_protocol`

## Recent Changes
- 034-schema-first-functions: Schema-first Functions V1.1 — one project module, `ActiveFunctionSet`, root runtime lease, shared `runtime.d.ts`, FlatBuffer JS-boundary transfer, V8-only runtime
- 033-unified-backend-pgwire: Direct `pgwire`; gRPC-style tx control via `BackendSessionManager`; US9 client catalog shims project from `system.*`
